{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes","id":1452982,"title":"[Aberrant] How would a powerful nova rate against dc universe characters villains or heroes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-20T13:07:27-07:00","id":1452982,"title":"[Aberrant] How would a powerful nova rate against dc universe characters villains or heroes?","content":"How would a powerful nova stack up in the dc universe? How would one fair if he/she was transported to dc universe?<br /> <br /> What is everyone s thoughts or ideas on the subject?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 06-20-2021, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T13:28:52-07:00","id":1452983,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that the Novas are closer to the power level of the Marvel Universe. Superman, Green Lantern, Dr. Fate, Captain Marvel, Zatanna, and several other DC heroes could physically destroy planet Earth. Far fewer Marvel characters or Novas could. Although many DC characters could be simulated with the Aberrant rule set, things like Wonder Woman's strength, Superman's invulnerability, Flash's speed, are all impossible to handle. However, characters like Thor, Hulk, Storm, Invisible Woman, Thing, and Quicksilver, are all doable as Novas. <br /> <br /> That said, Hawkman, Black Canary, Red Tornado, Plastic Man, Aquaman, Mera, Saturn Girl, Lightning Lad, Starfire, and Honeybee, are all easily handled by the Aberrant rule set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T13:38:40-07:00","id":1452986,"title":"","content":"Huh that's odd I always had the impression that there wasn't that much of a power difference between the marvel and dc universes. I mean supermans invulnerability isn't it just high toughness with a few armour tags but I suppose theres a lot of interpretation when it comes to comic superpowers. I mean personally I picture novas who are getting into higher power levels as been not unlike Dr Manhattan and in DC he up there in the power rankings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T14:08:03-07:00","id":1452989,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s interesting because Aberrant has one thing that DC and Marvel don\u2019t, Novas evolve quite fast, all Novas, not just our novas as PCs, it\u2019s part of the lore.<br /> <br /> By 2028 I would guess they would have issues to deal with Green Lantern or most of the main JL, but by Aberrant War I think it would be a tough fight even to Superman. A few exceptions, Pax and Mal are very powerful, like city destruction level at least in 2028, and Mal can probably destroy Earth easily by Aberrant War.<br /> <br /> My approach for character design is very low powered, I would put Spider Man on Q2 as well as most of the X-Man, the best X-Men, FF and Avengers would be on Q3-4 with a few Q5 (Phoenix, Magneto, Hulk, Thor, etc). MCU is one step lower probably, with Hulk and Thor around Q4 and Spider man as Q1. Super Soldiers are all Superiors, so Q0,5...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T14:36:10-07:00","id":1452991,"title":"","content":"The problem with answering your question is that power levels can fluctuate wildly based on the writer. One of the most recent versions of Superman received a power evaluation in a super science facility, and was informed he was lifting the equivalent weight of the planet Earth. The villainous Superboy Prime punched reality itself so hard that history changed. Over in Marvel Comics, Iceman has both frozen several miles worth of the Hudson River in a matter of seconds and been vaporized, condensed into rainwater, and reformed his body.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about making a starting Nova character, they're almost certain to pale in comparison to most established heroes and villains. As an example, consider a simple Brick character. Q4, Mega-Might 4, Toughness 4. That is 144 out of their 150 starting xp. They're as strong as a wrecking ball and as tough as reinforced concrete, but that isn't too impressive by the standards of your typical Brick. At that level, handgun fire can still theoretically harm them.<br /> <br /> OTOH, a sufficiently experienced Nova can potentially have a huge array of powers, with several of them at frankly ridiculous levels. They could utterly crush almost anyone below the cosmic tier combatants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T03:12:43-07:00","id":1453339,"title":"","content":"Starting Aberrants seem to be strong &quot;Marvel Team Members&quot; in terms of power. That is to say, outside Telepathy/Clairvoyance/Precognition powers - you could pretty easily make yourself a Fantastic Four or new addition to the X-Men line-up.<br /> <br /> Super soldiers &amp; the like are rather easy using the &quot;stealth nova&quot; type builds mentioned in the rulebook. The &quot;Superiors&quot; from the \u00c6xpansion book also work well for them, though personally I dislike the idea of &quot;social Superiors&quot; as social rules, bureaucracy, etiquette, etc are a bit too nebulous &amp; non-universal for my taste to have as &quot;enhanced human powers&quot;. (Just my opinion though.)<br /> <br /> Modern day Hulk, Thor, and other &quot;singular&quot; characters who only team up for global/cosmic threats are going to need decent experience (&amp; Transformations) to get an equivalent Aberrant character there in terms of power. You <b>can</b> get there but you'll be paying Flux/Transcendence costs for it.<br /> <br /> I think to get to the cosmic level characters (including Superman/Sentinel level paragons) is not possible within the rules &quot;as is&quot;. To get to their level of power - you are well beyond where Transcendence / Chrysalis pull you away from the human look &amp; mind-set they can present. Even with Dormancy at full dots, I see issues at this level.<br /> <br /> True godlike characters are impossible in current Aberrant without leaving humanity completely behind, and even then the powers list doesn't have the &quot;truly cosmic&quot; levels that Aberrant 1e did. Which is good in setting, but if you're looking at Aberrant for use as a generic super-heroes ruleset, it does come with some limitations. Ones I can (&amp; am happy to deal with) but they're there nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:22:12-07:00","id":1453348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453339#post1453339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think to get to the cosmic level characters (including Superman/Sentinel level paragons) is not possible within the rules &quot;as is&quot;. To get to their level of power - you are well beyond where Transcendence / Chrysalis pull you away from the human look &amp; mind-set they can present. Even with Dormancy at full dots, I see issues at this level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It is entirely possible to hit Quantum 9 with only Transcendence 6, which gives you two Low-Level Transformations, one Mid-Level Transformation, and a +3 Difficulty to form bonds with normal humans. Being an absent minded, blue skinned hero with a supersensitive sense of smell and difficulties relating to others is hardly an insurmountable problem. The Subtle Presence Mega-Edge even cancels some of those penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T15:42:08-07:00","id":1453411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453348#post1453348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being an absent minded, blue skinned hero with a supersensitive sense of smell and difficulties relating to others is hardly an insurmountable problem. The Subtle Presence Mega-Edge even cancels some of those penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's still not <i>&quot;Clark Kent who fits in fine at the Daily Planet&quot;</i>. Which is what I was talking about. You are no longer fitting in perfectly with the baselines despite having the powers of a god/cosmic threat - you stand out as different. The whole point of forced Transcendence is to make that so.<br /> <br /> And whilst &quot;Subtle Presence&quot; can make it so people don't notice you look like a smurf, you're still blue. That's not something Clark Kent has to deal with, though I reckon the man has some Subtle Presence going on to allow glasses to be all he needs for a disguise! \ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> That said, yes, you can get pretty strong within the rules... but Superman &amp; Sentry are top-tier outside purely cosmic threats in the DC / Marve universes and I'm pretty sure the <i>&quot;Power of a 1000 Suns&quot;</i> is pushing it for Aberrant. Admittedly, Sentry comes with Void (a Hyde persona transformation), but I still think Aberrant's cap is lower than the level these top-level paragons are able to demonstrate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26905,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","user":"Eternl Knight","date":". 06-24-2021, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T05:59:50-07:00","id":1453445,"title":"","content":"I agree with everyone else. I think Aberrant novas fit in better with the Marvel universe than the DC universe as far as power level and general style goes (though I think Batman would make a great darkstar nova).<br /> <br /> That being said, this guy I know who\u2019s been playing Aberrant a lot longer than I have told me he found a campaign journal online by Steve Kenson (one of the famous Aberrant 1e designers) where he does Spider-Man for the Aberrant universe. But he couldn\u2019t remember the site name and when I looked for it on Google I couldn\u2019t find it. (I think maybe Marvel made Steve Kenson take it down.)<br /> <br /> Gtg. Bye!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-25-2021, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T06:54:04-07:00","id":1453450,"title":"","content":"Batman definitely works better as a Talent than as a dark star nova.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T08:40:18-07:00","id":1453454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453450#post1453450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman definitely works better as a Talent than as a dark star nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Isn\u2019t a darkstar nova just a nova whose powers are so subtle they appear to be just a highly skilled baseline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T09:05:18-07:00","id":1453456,"title":"","content":"Yes. But I didn't say that Batman <i>can't</i> be modeled as a darkstar; I said that he works better as a Talent. And I stand by that claim: both conceptually and system-wise. <br /> <br /> In particular, a major reason why Batman is able to hold his own in the Justice League is his \u201cplot armor\u201d, which is basically Dramatic Editing. Unless you rely on Edges like Well-Equipped, a darkstar isn't going to have access to Dramatic Editing; and even then, the access is going to be far more limited than what Batman would have as a Talent. <br /> <br /> And conceptually, the idea is that Batman <i>doesn't</i> have any powers, not even subtle ones. True, he's unrealistically competent; but that's <i>also</i> a staple of Talents: they're all about people who get by on extraordinary luck, skill, and grit; that's Batman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T11:03:10-07:00","id":1453467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453445#post1453445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Steve Kenson (one of the famous Aberrant 1e designers)</div> </div> </div> </div>Steve Kenson was the lead designer on Trinity Continuum: Aberrant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> where he does Spider-Man for the Aberrant universe. But he couldn\u2019t remember the site name and when I looked for it on Google I couldn\u2019t find it. (I think maybe Marvel made Steve Kenson take it down.) </div> </div> </div>Eddy created Spider-Man during the Aberrant Kickstarter here: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aberrant/posts/2568785/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...posts/2568785/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T11:08:34-07:00","id":1453468,"title":"","content":"I think you mean &quot;Night Monkey&quot;... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 06-25-2021, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T13:21:14-07:00","id":1453475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453456#post1453456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. But I didn't say that Batman <i>can't</i> be modeled as a darkstar; I said that he works better as a Talent. And I stand by that claim: both conceptually and system-wise. <br /> <br /> In particular, a major reason why Batman is able to hold his own in the Justice League is his \u201cplot armor\u201d, which is basically Dramatic Editing. Unless you rely on Edges like Well-Equipped, a darkstar isn't going to have access to Dramatic Editing; and even then, the access is going to be far more limited than what Batman would have as a Talent. <br /> <br /> And conceptually, the idea is that Batman <i>doesn't</i> have any powers, not even subtle ones. True, he's unrealistically competent; but that's <i>also</i> a staple of Talents: they're all about people who get by on extraordinary luck, skill, and grit; that's Batman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I think you\u2019re right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T13:21:56-07:00","id":1453476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453467#post1453467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Steve Kenson was the lead designer on Trinity Continuum: Aberrant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eddy created Spider-Man during the Aberrant Kickstarter here: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aberrant/posts/2568785/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...posts/2568785/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome. Idk that. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T16:11:58-07:00","id":1453489,"title":"","content":"In contrast to Batman, Captain America and Ironman are arguably better handled as stealth novas: at least their movie versions. Steve Rogers could be described as having Mega-Might 1, Mega-Dexterity 1, and Mega-Stamina 1: his Supersoldier-enhanced physique clearly takes him beyond 99% of regular humans; but he's not <i>so</i> far beyond regular humans so as to be clearly <i>super</i>human. Ironman has Mega-Intellect with Instant Expert, Inventor, Perfectionist, Prodigy (Technology), and Q-Tech in the form of his armor. Outside of his suit, he's mostly mistaken for being a regular human. Contrast him with James Rhodes, who <i>is</i> a regular human (or maybe a Talent) outside of <i>his</i> suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T17:17:55-07:00","id":1453494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453411#post1453411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's still not <i>&quot;Clark Kent who fits in fine at the Daily Planet&quot;</i>. Which is what I was talking about. You are no longer fitting in perfectly with the baselines despite having the powers of a god/cosmic threat - you stand out as different. The whole point of forced Transcendence is to make that so.<br /> <br /> And whilst &quot;Subtle Presence&quot; can make it so people don't notice you look like a smurf, you're still blue. That's not something Clark Kent has to deal with, though I reckon the man has some Subtle Presence going on to allow glasses to be all he needs for a disguise! \ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> That said, yes, you can get pretty strong within the rules... but Superman &amp; Sentry are top-tier outside purely cosmic threats in the DC / Marve universes and I'm pretty sure the <i>&quot;Power of a 1000 Suns&quot;</i> is pushing it for Aberrant. Admittedly, Sentry comes with Void (a Hyde persona transformation), but I still think Aberrant's cap is lower than the level these top-level paragons are able to demonstrate.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Superman, Dormancy is a thing. (Yes, yes, we can quibble about how it is not <i>exactly the same thing</i>. The point is you can absolutely be a Q9 Nova who pretends to be human and has a day job.)<br /> <br /> Similarly, you can absolutely reach cosmic scale - most of the 'cosmic powers' from 1e can be handled by large amounts of Scale, frankly. The handful that can't (Universe Creation, Planck Scaling), can either be considered special cases of other powers or the kind of stuff a Quantum 10 nova can do. But if you want to sit here and tell me someone with a Scale 9 Quantum Attack who can blow up planets if they max out, or someone with Growth 9 who can reach Scale <i>10</i> &quot;I am comparable to a solar system&quot; size casually isn't &quot;cosmic threat&quot; level, I'm gonna say I don't understand your use of cosmic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T18:49:53-07:00","id":1453502,"title":"","content":"You can get a reasonable approximation of Superman at Scale 6, which corresponds to Transcendence 3, which is just under the limit where Transformations are required. If you think you can get away with one or two minor Transformations, you can get that Scale up to 8, which handles nearly everything that even DC's heroes can manage; only a rare few cases, like the Flash's ability to run at the speed of light, needs Scale 9. And frankly, much of the Scale 7+ feats that we see DC heroes performing aren't things that they do casually; a case could be made that these are examples of the Max Out rules, rather than power levels that these guys have purchased with experience and can use consistently. <br /> <br /> That said, I could see implementing a simple house rule to make DC-like characters much easier to implement in Aberrant: similar to how Maxing Out is a requirement to spend experience on increasing Quantum Traits, allow someone who engages game systems designed to remove Flux (mostly Grounding; but also Determination if you're using the Four-Color Tone) to spend experience on reducing Transcendence: say, for the same cost of gaining a point of Quantum, you can remove a point of Transcendence. This would make it possible to get all the way up to Quantum 10 without <i>any</i> Transcendence, if the character is willing to put in the time and effort to do so. Clark Kent, then, would be Superman making an effort to maintain a secret identity (Grounding) and making a special effort to avoid becoming distanced from humanity (spending experience to eliminate Transcendence). This matches a number of characterizations of Superman, such as his post-Crisis version, where he saw himself first and foremost as Clark Kent, with Superman being the public persona he took on in order to maintain a private life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T10:55:04-07:00","id":1453567,"title":"","content":"I really don't get why people can't see that these Superman's traits are simply Transformations/Aberrations due to high Quantum:<br /> 1) Requires Yellow Sun.<br /> 2) Vulnerable to Kryptonite.<br /> 3) Protections doesn't work against Magic.<br /> <br /> You could even argue that his &quot;Unmovable Morals&quot; is a Mental Aberration (since ALL versions of Superman are Morally Adamant, even if said morality is Dictatorship as in the Injustice games). Even when this behavior clearly is very troublesome for him or his friends.<br /> <br /> note: Clark's day job = Grounding. it can't be Dormancy, because the retains all Powers whilst he's behaving in &quot;Clark Kent mode&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T11:39:16-07:00","id":1453577,"title":"","content":"You have a point about Superman's Vulnerability to Kryptonite, and possibly a Power Loss (to gadgets that can bathe him in Red Solar Radiation); but ironically, I can't think of a pair of Minor Transformations that would apply: the problem with Inhuman Beauty is that it would only apply to Superman: the whole point of Clark Kent is that his appearance <i>isn't</i> unusual. <br /> <br /> Going back to my earlier suggestion: instead of letting a Nova lower her Transcendence, maybe they should just be able to buy off (or at least buy down) individual Transformations, as a sort of inverse of Body Modifications? Then I could see Superman as Quantum 8 with a Power Loss and Vulnerability Transformation, but having \u201csold off\u201d his Minor Transformations. That said, that would still leave him with Transcendence 5, which would apply a significant penalty to social interactions with baselines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T19:28:23-07:00","id":1453618,"title":"","content":"if you think about it, there's no problem with social penalties for Superman. As Clark Kent he's seen as clumsy and wimpy; as Superman he's seen as otherworldly good (or simply otherworldly) and people just can't relate to him as they would a &quot;normal person&quot;.<br /> <br /> for Minor, I'd go for: Psychological Shift (Static Morality); Feeding Requirement (Sunlight).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T20:07:43-07:00","id":1453621,"title":"","content":"That Feeding Requirement is something of a stretch: the point of the Transformation is that it's <i>not</i> something that's ubiquitous \u2014 which sunlight is; and while there's no sunlight at night, that doesn't bother Superman; he's got enough of a charge stored up at any given time that a night's worth of lack of sunlight doesn't even phase him. Times that he's depleted his solar reserves have been, say, weeks spent in interstellar space (e.g., the Superman/Aliens graphic novel) or after he was beaten to death by Doomsday, and the regeneration coffin basically extracted all of his solar reserves in the process of saving his life. Other than cases like that, Superman doesn't need to feed on sunlight in any meaningful way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T03:08:16-07:00","id":1453635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453567#post1453567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">note: Clark's day job = Grounding. it can't be Dormancy, because the retains all Powers whilst he's behaving in &quot;Clark Kent mode&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know the bit I said about quibbling? <i>This is that</i>.<br /> <br /> If we're implementing a concept into TC:Aberrant, which is <i>decidedly not</i> a generic superhero game, we have to permit some room to alter the concept to fit. <i>My</i> Clark Kent certainly does have Dormancy.<br /> <br /> If you want a 100% accurate comics-based take, HERO, Mutants and Masterminds, and friends are right down the street. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T05:16:12-07:00","id":1453640,"title":"","content":"In my view there is no way Clark is a Dormant Superman. He is not dormant in any way, he just plays stupid and clumsy to make him as distant from what he really is (Superman) as possible.<br /> <br /> Dormancy is about a version of the character with no powers but also not indentifiable as a Nova, more like Hulk x Banner (it\u2019s kind of extreme, but the best example), He-Man x Adan (still kind of different physically, but less extreme) or Lady Bug x Marinette (probably the best example of low level dormancy). They don\u2019t need to be really different, but when dormant the character has no access to powers and can\u2019t be identifiable as super no matter the way you measure it.<br /> <br /> Clark has his powers on all the time, Colossus is superstrong even when not in metal body, so they are not dormant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T07:23:06-07:00","id":1453646,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it more, Marvel, unlike DC, has tended to pull toward having fewer sources of Super Powers. DC tried that Metahuman thing for a while, and it made some logical sense, but it's long forgotten. The Aberrant setting has one basic source for all superpowers, Flux. Marvel doesn't come anywhere near that, but subsectors like the X-Men (they're all mutants) exposure to radiation covers a large part of the cast too (Spider Man and the Fantastic Four as examples),. Just think about alien influence, both extraterrestrial and ultraterrestial in the Marvel setting. Doctor Strange, the Inhumans, the Silver Surfer, Thor, Nova, and the Eternals all fit this paradigm in one way or another.,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-27-2021, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T08:12:31-07:00","id":1453652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453646#post1453646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it more, Marvel, unlike DC, has tended to pull toward having fewer sources of Super Powers. DC tried that Metahuman thing for a while, and it made some logical sense, but it's long forgotten. The Aberrant setting has one basic source for all superpowers, Flux. Marvel doesn't come anywhere near that, but subsectors like the X-Men (they're all mutants) exposure to radiation covers a large part of the cast too (Spider Man and the Fantastic Four as examples),. Just think about alien influence, both extraterrestrial and ultraterrestial in the Marvel setting. Doctor Strange, the Inhumans, the Silver Surfer, Nova, and the Eternal all fit this paradigm in one way or another.,</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T13:27:13-07:00","id":1453665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453640#post1453640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Colossus is superstrong even when not in metal body</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless they've changed how his powers work in the last few years. Colossus is very strong because he's 6'6&quot; and 250 lbs. of muscle in his base form, not because he has super strength. When he activates his power, he's 7'5&quot; and 500 lbs. of super strong and durable metal.<br /> <br /> This doesn't actually count as Dormancy since mutant detectors work on him whether he's armored up or not. He probably has Density 4 with the Non-Living, Duration, and possibly Reduced Cost tags. The Toughness granted by Density may have then Environmental and/or Hard Armor tags. The added 11&quot; of height are just a special effect and don't require an actual power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T14:53:18-07:00","id":1453669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1452986#post1452986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh that's odd I always had the impression that there wasn't that much of a power difference between the marvel and dc universes.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the whole no, in terms of who gets the most screentime very yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T21:56:12-07:00","id":1453892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453567#post1453567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't get why people can't see that these Superman's traits are simply Transformations/Aberrations due to high Quantum:<br /> 1) Requires Yellow Sun.<br /> 2) Vulnerable to Kryptonite.<br /> 3) Protections doesn't work against Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one of them I see being relevant at the gaming table is (perhaps) Kryptonite. And even then, it's debatable whether it's a mid-level transformation or not given the rarity of the substance. I'd grant it to a player I trusted for sure, but you'd better believe that almost every mastermind/nemesis is going to know about it (even if they cannot get a hold of it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453567#post1453567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could even argue that his &quot;Unmovable Morals&quot; is a Mental Aberration (since ALL versions of Superman are Morally Adamant, even if said morality is Dictatorship as in the Injustice games). Even when this behavior clearly is very troublesome for him or his friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, though I'd again have to say this doesn't often offer up much practical complications to Superman and especially not to Clark Kent. The point of the Transformation/Aberrations is to remove them from humanity and make it harder for them to hide their &quot;otherness&quot;. Being a &quot;boy scout&quot; only really is an issue if the character is meant to be running undercover black-ops or the like... which he isn't as he's Superman. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453567#post1453567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">note: Clark's day job = Grounding. it can't be Dormancy, because the retains all Powers whilst he's behaving in &quot;Clark Kent mode&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree completely. This one strikes me as trying to ignore a major component of the character simply to win an argument about whether Aberrant can accurately portray the character &quot;as is&quot; without hitting the brick wall of Aberrant's built-in balance mechanism of Transcendence/Transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T22:08:01-07:00","id":1453894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453635#post1453635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know the bit I said about quibbling? <i>This is that</i>.<br /> <br /> If we're implementing a concept into TC:Aberrant, which is <i>decidedly not</i> a generic superhero game, we have to permit some room to alter the concept to fit. <i>My</i> Clark Kent certainly does have Dormancy.<br /> <br /> If you want a 100% accurate comics-based take, HERO, Mutants and Masterminds, and friends are right down the street. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point here is that it's not actually quibbling in this context. The question asked wasn't <i>&quot;How would you build something close to DC/Marvel heroes in Aberrant?&quot;</i> so telling people they're quibbling for not sticking to some boundary conditions you decided to add is a bit abrupt. This Superman stuff is stemming (mostly) from my reply to the actual question asked. And the answer is, as you've determined &amp; seem to think is &quot;quibbling&quot;, that Superman <i>&quot;as fully represented in the comics&quot; </i>cannot be translated to Aberrant without hitting the brick wall of Transcendence/Transformation making him <b>unavoidably</b> other than baseline human in social situations.<br /> <br /> Dormancy has the downside of not actually having your powers when Dormant. A sniper can pick off a Dormant nova whereas Superman is ALWAYS invulnerable. Being &quot;clumsy &amp; wimpy&quot; is not a downside to Clark Kent because that is simply an act that can be shed at will, unlike Mental Aberrations which are permanent conditions affecting the character. And so on.<br /> <br /> The whole point of my answer (&amp; others responding since) is that Aberrant doesn't create super-heroes like Superman. You agree to that above, but seem to think if someone points it out themselves, that's &quot;quibbling&quot;. It's not. It's the point. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T23:32:10-07:00","id":1453896,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that's why I suggested that if you want to use Aberrant to more accurately reflect the likes of Superman, you should bend the rules a bit. And the simplest solution I can think of (that is, the smallest change needed to allow the desired result) would be to let Novas use Grounding as a catalyst to buy off Transformations and/or Transcendence. <br /> <br /> And frankly, I'd like more flexibility with Transformations. Being forced to take two minor, then two moderate, then two major ones is far too rigid for my taste. Something as simple as being allowed to replace a minor with a moderate instead of taking another minor, or replacing a moderate with a major instead of taking another moderate, would help out considerably: someone could still have just one Transformation (albeit a major one) as high up as Transcendence 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T07:01:41-07:00","id":1453930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453896#post1453896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; that's why I suggested that if you want to use Aberrant to more accurately reflect the likes of Superman, you should bend the rules a bit. And the simplest solution I can think of (that is, the smallest change needed to allow the desired result) would be to let Novas use Grounding as a catalyst to buy off Transformations and/or Transcendence.<br /> <br /> And frankly, I'd like more flexibility with Transformations. Being forced to take two minor, then two moderate, then two major ones is far too rigid for my taste. Something as simple as being allowed to replace a minor with a moderate instead of taking another minor, or replacing a moderate with a major instead of taking another moderate, would help out considerably: someone could still have just one Transformation (albeit a major one) as high up as Transcendence 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like more flexibility, but this one is unfortunately of the table... if I remember correctly, minor Aberrations automatically become worse when your Transcendence grows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T08:14:40-07:00","id":1453937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453930#post1453930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like more flexibility, but this one is unfortunately of the table... if I remember correctly, minor Aberrations automatically become worse when your Transcendence grows.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They are still the same, MAYBE you can say they are a bit more overt, but they still work the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T10:09:52-07:00","id":1453947,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think that if your goal is to create &quot;Supers&quot; that doesn't really have Transcendence and Transformation problems intrinsic to Novas, you should simply create an XP table with these costs (beware &quot;N&quot; isn't necessarily the same in each case; i'ts just a placeholder here).<br /> <br /> +N XP = &quot;Don't get a Transcendence Point&quot; tax (add to the cost of something that would get you a Transcendence point; probably Quantum Trait)<br /> +N XP = &quot;Don't get a Low-Level Transformation&quot; tax (add to cost of something that would get you this transformation)<br /> +N XP = &quot;Don't get a Mid-Level Transformation&quot; tax (add to cost of something that would get you this transformation)<br /> +N XP = &quot;Don't get a High-Level Transformation&quot; tax (add to cost of something that would get you this transformation)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T10:52:16-07:00","id":1453952,"title":"","content":"That's essentially what I'm thinking \u2014 except that TC:Ab has a requirement in it that buying up your Quantum abilities requires pushing your powers; so it seems appropriate to me to put a similar requirement on spending experience to delay or reverse Transcendence or Transformations. Tying it to Grounding does that, and nicely reinforces the thematic element that the Novas who remain engaged in mundane life tend to be the ones who remain the most human. <br /> <br /> As for what \u201cN\u201d is, my logic is that: <br /> \u2022 not gaining a point of X should cost the same as removing a point of X. (Or maybe it should be cheaper?)<br /> \u2022 removing a point of Transcendence should cost the same as buying a point of Quantum. <br /> \u2022 removing a minor Transformation should cost the same as buying a point of Body Modification \u2014 or, more generally, a single Mega-Edge. <br /> \u2022 downgrading a moderate Transformation to a minor one, or a major one to a moderate one, should cost the same as removing a minor one. <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think that you should be able to \u201cundo\u201d Transcendence and Transformations after the fact, not just prevent yourself from gaining them in the first place. Though upon reflection, I could see an argument for the former to be harder to do than the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T18:19:40-07:00","id":1454028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453930#post1453930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like more flexibility, but this one is unfortunately of the table... if I remember correctly, minor Aberrations automatically become worse when your Transcendence grows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to my knowledge and I've been reading &amp; re-reading that section of Aberrant in light of this conversation. You simply keep the minor transformation and add more transformations on top as required by Transcendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T19:07:44-07:00","id":1454031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453947#post1453947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think that if your goal is to create &quot;Supers&quot; that doesn't really have Transcendence and Transformation problems intrinsic to Novas, you should simply create an XP table with these costs...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453952#post1453952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's essentially what I'm thinking \u2014 except that TC:Ab has a requirement in it that buying up your Quantum abilities requires pushing your powers; so it seems appropriate to me to put a similar requirement on spending experience to delay or reverse Transcendence or Transformations. Tying it to Grounding does that, and nicely reinforces the thematic element that the Novas who remain engaged in mundane life tend to be the ones who remain the most human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these ideas for house-ruled campaigns/settings having a more &quot;four colours&quot; feel to them. It makes Superman(-like characters) far more than a collection of super powers - they're also made a <b>heavy</b> investment in keeping themselves &quot;human&quot;. They've decided that Transcendence is something to be avoided at all costs so are spending a lot of time &amp; effort keeping &quot;grounded&quot; alongside the people they're protecting / hiding amongst.<br /> <br /> It also allows for stories that push the narrative that there are shortcuts to power, but they can cost you everything. Say the Superman analogue decides to save the President instead of some poor guy's wife (say due to a Sadistic Choice trope decision). In his grief, the widower erupts as a Nova and decides to enact vengeance... but it would take years (decades?) to push himself to the level of his chosen nemesis (all the while, Superman analogue is <i>also</i> getting stronger)... but he could forgo his humanity to get there quicker.<br /> <br /> Rules as written mean that Superman becomes as monsterous / inhuman as his nemesis over time (&amp; stronger as well). With a setting house-rule though, Superman remains a boy scout hiding amongst humanity because he keeps feeding his XP into staying &quot;human&quot;(ish) whilst his Doomsday analogue grows ever stronger &amp; more monstrous to take him on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1453952#post1453952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do</i> think that you should be able to \u201cundo\u201d Transcendence and Transformations after the fact, not just prevent yourself from gaining them in the first place. Though upon reflection, I could see an argument for the former to be harder to do than the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping with usual story tropes - I agree they should be harder to buy off than to just initially avoid. In cases like this, think of the Transformations like a loan. You've reaped some benefits in the past/present from either buying power/edge/quantum cheaper &amp;/or having pushed yourself beyond your limits to win a challenge you otherwise would have lost. You don't just pay off that loan XP-for-XP, it comes with interest. I'd even stipulate in my games that the longer you've had the Transformation, the more it costs to get rid of it. Interest accumulates and it works with the story tropes we're dealing with.<br /> <br /> Thing about it. In the comics, supers will occasionally push themselves beyond their limits &amp;/or get a power booost and as a result they start to vibrate too fast, eyes glow, have flame auras, etc until they can pull themselves together, get better control of their powers, etc. That represents the standard <i>&quot;buying off Transcendence/Transformation as soon as possible&quot;</i> scenario. On the other hand, heroes with Transformations they've had since becoming empowered (e.g. bought at character gen) or simply allowed themselves to have for a long time are always harder for them to buy off in story - often needing more than just self control (e.g. gene mods, psychic therapy, etc) which represent a higher XP cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T19:48:26-07:00","id":1454036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1454031#post1454031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping with usual story tropes - I agree they should be harder to buy off than to just initially avoid. In cases like this, think of the Transformations like a loan. You've reaped some benefits in the past/present from either buying power/edge/quantum cheaper &amp;/or having pushed yourself beyond your limits to win a challenge you otherwise would have lost. You don't just pay off that loan XP-for-XP, it comes with interest. I'd even stipulate in my games that the longer you've had the Transformation, the more it costs to get rid of it. Interest accumulates and it works with the story tropes we're dealing with.<br /> <br /> Thing about it. In the comics, supers will occasionally push themselves beyond their limits &amp;/or get a power booost and as a result they start to vibrate too fast, eyes glow, have flame auras, etc until they can pull themselves together, get better control of their powers, etc. That represents the standard <i>&quot;buying off Transcendence/Transformation as soon as possible&quot;</i> scenario. On the other hand, heroes with Transformations they've had since becoming empowered (e.g. bought at character gen) or simply allowed themselves to have for a long time are always harder for them to buy off in story - often needing more than just self control (e.g. gene mods, psychic therapy, etc) which represent a higher XP cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned awhile back that comic book supers often undergo major transformations that'll last for a few story arcs before things (usually) return to the status quo. Some examples off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Spider-Man gaining six arms.<br /> The Wasp turning into a humanoid insect.<br /> Namorita during her Kymaera phase, when she had black eyes, webbed hands, shark-like projections on her calves, and the standard blue Atlantean skin.<br /> Superman, who was a blue electric being for awhile.<br /> <br /> I suggested at the time that heroes who use the option to buy new traits at a reduced xp cost via transformations could later pay the xp difference and perform some major personal task in order to shed those transformations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T06:13:56-07:00","id":1454126,"title":"","content":"We're on the same page. I'm saying &quot;more XP based on time&quot;, you're saying &quot;major personal task&quot;. We're both saying &quot;something extra to count as 'interest' on the XP loan the Transformation initially paid for&quot;.<br /> <br /> I do think that player choice should come into it somewhat. Got the Transformation from accidentally pushing Flux over 10 and gaining Transcendence? OK, you've got the Transformation until you buy your Transcendence down a level (so long as that is your next XP spend). Chose to buy a visible mutation just to get that Quantum point cheaper? That's going to have a &quot;easy route tax&quot; to buy off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T06:44:14-07:00","id":1454128,"title":"","content":"I think we're all in the same page. Maybe I'll think about actual XP costs later (for this kind of world in which you can get rid of Transformations), but there's a last point I'd like to mention: if your goal is to build &lt;a game world&gt; like Marvel or DC, in which Transcendence/Transformations/etc are not the norm, but the exception (e.g. if for superpowered people the rule is to be Reed Richards and the exception is to be The Thing), maybe the best house rule should be &quot;High Quantum does NOT give you Transcendence automatically&quot;. This way, only characters that really WANT aberrations or Transcendence social penalties would have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T13:41:40-07:00","id":1454152,"title":"","content":"How many characters actually qualify as high enough in Quantum that they need a significant amount of Transcendence? You can hit Quantum 7 - which is one scale more powerful than a nuclear bomb - before gaining your first Low-Level Transformation, and that can easily be a &quot;Psychological Shift&quot; which is completely in line with typical comic character behavior. That same character would have a +2 Difficulty to form bonds with regular people, but short term train wreck relationships with the non-powered are also common in comics.<br /> <br /> Anyone short of god-tier heroes and super speedsters will presumably top out at Quantum 6, and never need to gain Transformations at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T00:20:59-07:00","id":1454179,"title":"","content":"Agree with Shepherdboi, and I would say more. You can have a Q9 Nova with 3 psychological transformations (2 minor and one medium), that would seam perfectly common for someone that can obliterate Star systems with simple actions (what is Megalomaniac if you already have Q9?).<br /> <br /> Superman is an example, Clark is is view of how a human should behave next to him, a weakling, clumsy and with a very shy personality, and he really believe he is unbeatable to the point he never uses his total power, not even when near defeat (and so far a very small number of creatures in the universe proved him wrong), he has a serious psychological disorder, and the Boy Scout aspect is part of it.<br /> <br /> Also some minor transformations are pretty common in superheroes, aberrant eyes, unnatural skin tones, weird hair (but we can point to the 80s for that hair styles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T07:30:30-07:00","id":1454201,"title":"","content":"I would argue that Superman <i>doesn't</i> have psychological transformations, and definitely isn't Transcendence 6 (+3 difficulty on all social interactions with regular humans). Part of what makes him who he is is that he's remarkably well-adjusted, and <i>doesn't</i> have psychological oddities; his coffee of ethics is <i>not</i> a psychological disorder. <br /> <br /> I have trouble seeing him as even Transcendence 4 (+2 difficulty when interacting with regular humans). <i>Batman</i> is more socially awkward than Superman is, who <i>isn't</i> socially awkward. I could see Superman as low as Quantum 7, with his more outlandish feats being achieved through Maxing Out; but even that mandates an unacceptable high Transcendence score for him. Thus, the need for a rules hack for games that feature Superman-like Novas that makes Transcendence something you can avoid entirely if you put in the requisite effort to remaining grounded in everyday life (which Superman definitely does).<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm going to spin this off into a separate thread, as it really is a massive derail of this topic <i>and</i> is something I'd like to link to in one of my sig pages for future reference, which would be awkward at best as things stand.<br /> <br /> Update: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454210-avoiding-transcendence\">the page is up</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-04-2021, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T08:45:35-07:00","id":1454206,"title":"","content":"A note on Superman that might fit this discussion. Superman was reveled in the 1970s to unconsciously use his super hypnotic powers. Basically, Superman was unaware that he was unconsciously sending out a hypnotic order to everyone around him to see Clark as weak and a little sickly. In other words Supes was both unconsciously mind controlling other people to his advantage but self-sabotaging his attempts to lead a normal human life. <br /> <br /> Have fun with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T05:03:34-07:00","id":1454274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452982-aberrant-how-would-a-powerful-nova-rate-against-dc-universe-characters-villains-or-heroes?p=1454206#post1454206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A note on Superman that might fit this discussion. Superman was reveled in the 1970s to unconsciously use his super hypnotic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Supes has evolved bit since the 70's. Most heroes have really.<br /> <br /> Modern day Clark Kent is not really seen as weak/wimpy. He's not your go to for masculine macho heroism, sure, but he's seen as smart, capable, and as brave as any other regular guy. That's really the thing. Clark Kent is seen as normal. So normal he's forgettable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}